+## 2026-05-19 00:52:55 +03 - BE-0518
+- What was implemented
+  - Added the stable backend validation error code `E_VALIDATION` to the shared error registry, backend API taxonomy, HTTP status mapping, and documentation URL path.
+  - Switched `apierr.InvalidInput` and `apierr.Invalid` to emit `E_VALIDATION` while preserving the existing field-violation sorting, hint, redaction, and `ViolationsOf` behavior.
+  - Updated backend handler, store, worker, Dokploy, pagination, validate, and OpenAPI contract tests/prose that assert backend validation responses so they expect `E_VALIDATION`.
+  - Marked `BE-0518` as passing in `ralph/prd.json`.
+- Files changed
+  - `internal/errors/errors.go`, `internal/errors/errors_test.go`
+  - `internal/controlplane/apierr/*`, `internal/controlplane/apienvelope/*`
+  - Backend validation contract tests and backend OpenAPI/guidance prose under `internal/controlplane/**`
+  - `ralph/prd.json`
+- Verification run
+  - `gofmt -w .`
+  - `goimports -w .` was not run because `goimports` is not installed.
+  - `go mod tidy`
+  - `go test ./...`
+  - `go test -race ./...`
+  - `go vet ./...`
+  - `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`
+  - `go test -race ./internal/controlplane/...`
+  - `go test -run TestMigrations ./...`
+  - `go test -run TestPolicyMatrix ./...`
+  - `go test -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...`
+  - `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`
+  - `golangci-lint run ./...`
+- Results
+  - All executed checks passed. `golangci-lint` reported 0 issues.
+  - `staticcheck` and `govulncheck` were not installed.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups
+  - CLI-facing invalid-input behavior remains on `E_INVALID_INPUT`; this story only changes backend API validation errors emitted through `apierr`.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Backend validation contract changes are broad because many endpoint/store tests pin the public error code directly; update `apierr`, `apienvelope`, OpenAPI prose, and all backend contract assertions together.
+  - Keep `E_INVALID_INPUT` available for CLI/legacy non-backend callers while `apierr.InvalidInput` is the backend chokepoint for `E_VALIDATION`.
+---

